{"authored" [{"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & =\\frac{50-10\\sqrt{25}}{25-25}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})}{x-25} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})(x+5\\sqrt{x})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{(5\\sqrt{x})}^{2})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-25x)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x(x-25)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x}{x+5\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(25)}{25+5\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/ea