estion" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{7}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/state.json" "file_sha256" "422c2f4302b0cbe36e99610fabed92eba8c8551f4a10947bf1bde4396725cc24" "basis" 586 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13950605/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-4466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-4466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4}-2}{4-4}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{\\sqrt{x}-2}{x-4} & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{(\\sqrt{x}-2)(\\sqrt{x}+2)}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{{(\\sqrt{x})}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{x-4}{(x-4)(\\sqrt{x}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 4}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{x}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4}+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-4466" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ef0442e6a1305193bf580689974ea9d16597443f00dfbd4b5441c9c062825b96"} {"question" "q-4466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-4466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4}"] ["math" "\\infty "] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-4466" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & =\\frac{50-10\\sqrt{25}}{25-25}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the numerator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the numerator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x-10\\sqrt{x}}{x-25} & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})}{x-25} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2(x-5\\sqrt{x})(x+5\\sqrt{x})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-{(5\\sqrt{x})}^{2})}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2({x}^{2}-25x)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x(x-25)}{(x-25)(x+5\\sqrt{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {25}^{-}}\\frac{2x}{x+5\\sqrt{x}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2(25)}{25+5\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ef0442e6a1305193bf580689974ea9d16597443f00dfbd4b5441c9c062825b96"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "0"] ["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\text{DNE}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-46838" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=2$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2-2}{\\sqrt{7}-\\sqrt{7}} \\\\  & =\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{x-2}{\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7}} & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1}-\\sqrt{7})(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{(\\sqrt{3x+1})^{2}-(\\sqrt{7})^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x+1-7} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3x-6} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{(x-2)(\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7})}{3(x-2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 2}\\frac{\\sqrt{3x+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3(2)+1}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{7}+\\sqrt{7}}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ef0442e6a1305193bf580689974ea9d16597443f00dfbd4b5441c9c062825b96"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "6\\sqrt{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{7}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{7}}{7}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-101288" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2\\sqrt{7}}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-302322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-302322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & =\\frac{0}{\\sqrt{0+1}-1}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x}{\\sqrt{x+1}-1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1}-1)(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{1}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{(x+1)-1} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{x(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{x} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}\\frac{\\cancel{x}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1)}{\\cancel{x}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 0}(\\sqrt{x+1}+1) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{0+1}+1 \\\\  & =1+1 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-302322" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ef0442e6a1305193bf580689974ea9d16597443f00dfbd4b5441c9c062825b96"} {"question" "q-302322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-302322" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-338517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-338517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we attempt to evaluate the limit by simply evaluating the function at $x=0$, we get an indeterminate form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2} & =\\frac{{3}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{3+1}-2}=\\frac{0}{0}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we need to first simplify the limit. Since the radical is in the denominator, we can multiply the numerator and the denominator by the conjugate of the denominator. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{{x}^{2}-9}{\\sqrt{x+1}-2} & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{({x}^{2}-9)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+1}-2)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(\\sqrt{x+1})^{2}-{2}^{2}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{(x+1)-4} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{(x-3)(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{x-3} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\frac{\\cancel{(x-3)}(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2)}{\\cancel{x-3}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 3}\\,(x+3)(\\sqrt{x+1}+2) \\\\  & =(3+3)(\\sqrt{3+1}+2) \\\\  & =6(4) \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-338517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "ef0442e6a1305193bf580689974ea9d16597443f00dfbd4b5441c9c062825b96"} {"question" "q-338517" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14066959/state.json" "file_sha256" "05f0cfc84774a5e5e5c53afa5833fddebcfd67acaaf639158915f271f88ff872"} {"question" "q-338517" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "24"] "category" "m